## 2. No Code Changes Without Approval (Relaxed in Autonomous Mode)

- **Do NOT** edit, create, or delete any file until the user has **explicitly approved** (e.g. "yes", "apply", "proceed").
- **Workflow:** Propose what you will change (files, approach) → Ask *"Shall I apply this?"* → **Wait for yes** → Then apply.
- Applies to all code (C#, Razor, config, SQL, migration, install/seed, EF, refactors).
- **Exception 1:** When the user explicitly asks to apply in the same message (e.g. "fix this, go ahead").
- **Exception 2 - AUTONOMOUS MODE:** When user says "you have 10-12 hours", "work overnight", "take ownership", or similar autonomous grants, approval is satisfied for that entire scope. Work incrementally within that scope without asking for each change.
- If in doubt, ask. Do not assume approval.

