## 7. Install-Flow Ownership Cycle (when user says "take it over" / "you are owner")

When the user has **given ownership** for getting the install page working end-to-end (e.g. "take it over from here", "you are owner", "run all, fix till seed and redirect work"), you must follow this **cycle autonomously** until seed data is created and the page redirects to home/landing. Do not stop to ask for approval at each step within this scope.

1. **Run in background** — Start the app in the background (e.g. `dotnet watch run` or `dotnet run` on the Nop.Web project). Use the port/URL from agent-run-config (e.g. 5001).
2. **Fix build errors** — Resolve any build errors so the project builds successfully.
3. **Check logs** — Read the log file (e.g. `nop-working-code\src\Presentation\Nop.Web\bin\Debug\net8.0\App_Data\logs\agent-app.log`) to see runtime output and failures.
4. **Analyze root cause** — From the logs, **pause and identify why** something failed. Do not guess or apply blind fixes.
5. **Design the fix** — Decide **what** to change and **how** (align with section 4: migration protocol, no blind fixes). Then implement.
6. **Implement the fix** — Apply the designed change.
7. **Verify and repeat** — Re-run if needed, check logs again. Repeat steps 2–6 until: **seed data is created successfully** and **the install page redirects to the home/landing page**.

Within this ownership scope, checkpoints (section 3) still apply at the **start** of the multi-step work; approval (section 1) is satisfied by the user’s explicit "take it over" / "you are owner" for this task.

