## 8. Logging & Documentation Requirements

### **Logging Strategy:**
- Add comprehensive debug logs for every component
- Log initialization, data fetching, rendering
- Use existing Serilog setup (logs to `agent-app.log`)
- **Always log before/after critical operations**

**Example:**
```csharp
// .NET 8.0: Converted from [ChildActionOnly] action to ViewComponent
// Legacy: Html.Action("Logo", "Common")
// Modern: @await Component.InvokeAsync("Logo")
_logger.LogDebug("LogoViewComponent: Starting initialization");
_logger.LogDebug("LogoViewComponent: Store ID = {StoreId}", _storeContext.CurrentStore.Id);

try {
    // ... component logic ...
    _logger.LogInformation("LogoViewComponent: Successfully rendered logo for store {StoreName}", storeName);
} catch (Exception ex) {
    _logger.LogError(ex, "LogoViewComponent: Failed to render logo");
    throw;
}
```

### **Code Comments for .NET 8.0 Migrations:**
- Document WHY we changed from .NET 4.5.1 approach
- Mark legacy vs. modern patterns
- Explain ViewComponent conversions

**Example:**
```csharp
// MIGRATION NOTE (.NET 4.5.1 → 8.0):
// Legacy used [ChildActionOnly] public ActionResult Logo()
// .NET 8.0: Use ViewComponent pattern instead
// Reason: Html.Action() not supported in ASP.NET Core
// Reference: nopCommerce 4.70.0 CommonViewComponent pattern

public class LogoViewComponent : NopViewComponent
{
    // Constructor with DI (same as legacy, but cleaner)
    // Legacy used EngineContext.Current.Resolve<T>()
    // Modern uses constructor injection
    public LogoViewComponent(IStoreContext storeContext, ...)
    {
        // ...
    }
}
```

